1
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:22,980
Summer has come again this year.

2
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:24,960
It's here, it's here, it's really here.

3
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:25,200
Come on!

4
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,480
Big water, drink it all up, yajukui no

5
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:31,360
Water, it's water, it's water!

6
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:34,400
Big chest, make it a chest,
stick to the chest, yajukui no

7
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:35,780
Agesame

8
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:37,420
Purupuru purupuru purupuru purupuru

9
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:40,780
Summer has come again this year.

10
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:43,440
It's here, here, here, here,
here, here, here, here, here!

11
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:46,700
Summer has come again this year.

12
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:49,180
Geta! Geta! Geta! Geta! Geta! Bon! Bashi!

13
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:52,220
Big wave, small wave,
tiny wave, about that size

14
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:55,000
Poi in the southern breeze

15
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,280
Big Yoshiri, small Yoshiri,
tiny Yoshiri, about that size

16
00:00:58,280 --> 00:00:59,560
Akisori

17
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:21,120


18
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:38,600
Go, Takanoyama!

19
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:41,400
Look, there, right there!
Go all out and push him!

20
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:43,400
Yeah, yeah!

21
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:45,880
That's it, that's it!
Go for that left-hand grip of yours!

22
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:47,640
Takanoyama!

23
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:49,960
Aah! He did it, he did it!

24
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:53,720
Takanoyama?

25
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:57,880
That was a truly powerful bout.

26
00:01:58,060 --> 00:02:01,360
Takanoyama of Imahashi is unquestionably the champion,
isn't he.

27
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:09,380
I just didn't want to miss a single
bout of Grand Champion Takanoyama.

28
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:11,820
Watching it on TV...

29
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:15,140
you can't really grasp the true appeal of professional sumo,
can you?

30
00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:20,780
Well, have you ever seen
the real thing, then?

31
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:23,140
If it's a real sumo wrestler,

32
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:25,320
I sometimes see them
walking around in yukata.

33
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:27,720
I've seen that much myself.

34
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:29,400
Even though it's such a formal style,

35
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:31,640
why don't you go see the real thing?

36
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:35,420
Grand sumo tickets aren't that easy to get,
you know.

37
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:37,940
Is that so? I didn't know.

38
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:43,980
Even the cheapest seats at the Kokugikan are nearly
impossible to get without serious connections.

39
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:50,120
Watching grand sumo from the cheap seats
at the Kokugikan has been my lifelong dream.

40
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:53,080
The cheap seats are your lifelong dream

41
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:58,560
Come to think of it, didn't you get a pair of
tickets through the shopping district's raffle?

42
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:03,480
Ah, hey, senpai!

43
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,180
Where are you going?

44
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:07,100
Patrol, I'm on patrol!

45
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:13,114
Oh my, Ryo-chan leaving his soup behind,

46
00:03:13,164 --> 00:03:14,880
that's a rare thing indeed.

47
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:18,025
Come on, come on,

48
00:03:18,075 --> 00:03:21,480
it's the big summer sale lottery
at the Kamiari shopping street!

49
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:24,080
First prize is tickets to
the grand sumo tournament!

50
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:26,520
Seats at the very back of the final day,
no less!

51
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:29,060
It hasn't come out yet,
it hasn't come out yet!

52
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:31,420
Aaaah, service dog, service dog!

53
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:41,180
Hey, there's quite a few lying around Wait, this is bad,
Mass-production is trying to run the lottery!

54
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:48,980
Oh no, we have to stop today, this is too reckless!
What's wrong with Mass-production, don't you know?

55
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:51,862
That guy has incredibly good luck,

56
00:03:51,912 --> 00:03:53,982
the day before yesterday it
was a trip around Hokkaido,

57
00:03:54,032 --> 00:03:56,247
last year a four-day trip to Guam,

58
00:03:56,297 --> 00:03:59,260
and he won a personal
computer as a runner-up prize.

59
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:00,000
Hey!

60
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:05,660
You don't need to wrap things up
just because you won something. Here.

61
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,740
Right, let's go.

62
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:12,440
Aaaaah!

63
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:19,980
(unclear)

64
00:04:19,980 --> 00:04:22,920
He's on a roll

65
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:30,160
Aaaaah, the damn guy hit it again!

66
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:33,140
Yay, nice!

67
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,420
Senpai's already back?

68
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:39,360
Well, yeah.

69
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:42,760
You probably just wandered around somewhere,
didn't you?

70
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:43,880
Oh yeah?

71
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:46,760
Is it really okay to say that?

72
00:04:51,180 --> 00:04:52,840
Whoops, silly me.

73
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:55,940
I dropped the sumo tickets.

74
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:57,160
What?

75
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:59,860
W-what happened to that?

76
00:04:59,860 --> 00:05:00,280
That's...

77
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:03,880
Heh heh heh,
I've got connections everywhere, you know.

78
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:07,940
R-Ryotsu, you're amazing.

79
00:05:08,420 --> 00:05:10,360
Not really.

80
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:13,800
So, that is um...

81
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:16,183
Heh. Well, what do you think?
What do you think?

82
00:05:16,233 --> 00:05:18,840
Anyone want to buy these tickets?

83
00:05:19,140 --> 00:05:23,058
Sumo is Japan's national sport. For flowers,
cherry blossoms; for mountains, Fuji.

84
00:05:23,108 --> 00:05:26,560
You can't call yourself
Japanese if you don't watch sumo.

85
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:26,680
Meow!

86
00:05:27,380 --> 00:05:28,520
Hey, you there, mister!

87
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:31,580
Haven't you forgotten
the Japanese spirit lately

88
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:33,000
That said,

89
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:36,860
this is a ticket for the cheapest seats,
and for the final day at that.

90
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:42,140
It's not the kind of thing you can buy
on an ordinary salaryman's pay, is it?

91
00:05:42,620 --> 00:05:45,900
Is he not here? Is he not here?

92
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:47,580
Looks like he isn't here.

93
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:51,320
Oh well. Then, Nakagawa Reiko,
let's go watch it together.

94
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:52,500
Y-yes.

95
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:54,780
Only one person left.

96
00:05:57,420 --> 00:05:59,540
Right, I forgot the most important person!

97
00:06:01,340 --> 00:06:03,640
We have to invite the ramen shop owner too.

98
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:07,760
Senpai, you're going too far.

99
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:10,600
Yeah, that's a bit sneaky of you.

100
00:06:11,180 --> 00:06:12,660
Just kidding, just kidding.

101
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:15,880
Of course we'd invite the Chief,
who's always looking after us!

102
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,220
Chief, you're coming too, right?

103
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:23,320
Well, if you're inviting me,
I'd love to see it.

104
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:27,280
Speaking of which, Chief,
didn't you have some fine brandy?

105
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:29,920
The one you bragged about
getting as a summer gift?

106
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:31,100
That one...

107
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:34,960
Brandy drunk neat must be
absolutely delicious, I bet.

108
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:38,880
Fine, I'll bring it, I'll bring it.

109
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:40,760
Alright, that's settled, then!

110
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:42,660
Now, back to work, back to work!

111
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:46,080
The admission fee has turned out pretty expensive,
hasn't it?

112
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:48,340
It can't be helped at this point.

113
00:06:57,280 --> 00:06:59,700
Wow, I'm feeling kind of excited, aren't I?

114
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:02,300
Still, what a huge crowd there is.

115
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:06,000
Yeah, and the Kokugikan is really big,
isn't it?

116
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:09,900
After all,
it's Japan's national sport, isn't it?

117
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:11,660
Excuse me.

118
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:16,020
I'm sorry.

119
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:17,900
What a beauty!

120
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:20,969
Ah, this is no problem.

121
00:07:21,019 --> 00:07:22,860
Yeah, no problem.

122
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:25,220
Thank you.

123
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:28,240
Hey.

124
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:29,560
Bye.

125
00:07:30,820 --> 00:07:33,400
There are so many foreign visitors here too,
aren't there?

126
00:07:34,589 --> 00:07:38,120
sumo's popularity has become
quite international these days.

127
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,894
This internationally popular sumo,

128
00:07:40,944 --> 00:07:44,340
getting to watch it from the cheap seats feeling like a feudal lord,
no less,

129
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:47,720
well, well,
I wonder who we have to thank for that?

130
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:51,100
Speaking of which, the other day
at the shopping street lottery,

131
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:54,000
someone won tickets for the cheap seats,
didn't they?

132
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:54,620
Gh -

133
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:58,460
Yeah, yeah, I heard you were
some uniformed cop or something.

134
00:07:58,460 --> 00:07:59,700
W-what?

135
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:03,360
So what if I was?

136
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:06,680
If you're unhappy with lottery tickets,
you can always go home.

137
00:08:07,860 --> 00:08:10,620
No, no, lottery or not,

138
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:12,880
we're still getting to see sumo.

139
00:08:14,340 --> 00:08:15,700
I really am grateful to you.

140
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:18,360
Well then, shall we go?

141
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:20,280
Everyone has their tickets, right?

142
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:21,480
Yes.

143
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:24,560
Good. Follow close behind me, all of you.

144
00:08:28,660 --> 00:08:29,940
My tickets

145
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:31,320
Hey, wait!

146
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:35,640
You idiot!

147
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:40,840
The Ryogoku breeze is doing us a real favor,
isn't it?

148
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:43,480
Now the three of us can watch in comfort.

149
00:08:44,340 --> 00:08:46,740
Forget that guy.
Come on, let's go, let's go!

150
00:08:46,740 --> 00:08:48,160
Hah...

151
00:08:49,140 --> 00:08:50,480
H-hey, look over there!

152
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:52,420
Yay!

153
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:56,000
Thank goodness the Sumida
River's current was gentle!

154
00:08:56,180 --> 00:08:58,200
Wait, you jumped into the Sumida River?

155
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,460
Of course I did!

156
00:08:59,780 --> 00:09:02,100
I wasn't about to lose my precious tickets!

157
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:05,360
Honestly, what an unbelievable guy.

158
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:29,600
Look at them go, look at them go.

159
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:32,960
Nothing beats seeing it live, really.

160
00:09:33,780 --> 00:09:34,660
This way.

161
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:36,940
It's pretty cramped, isn't it.

162
00:09:36,940 --> 00:09:39,280
Well, but we're close to the ring.

163
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:40,860
Excellent, excellent.

164
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:43,580
What's that?

165
00:09:44,340 --> 00:09:45,900
It's snacks and sake.

166
00:09:45,900 --> 00:09:47,540
That's thoughtful.

167
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:49,100
Just what you'd expect from the cheap seats.

168
00:09:49,640 --> 00:09:51,560
Apparently they're handing out
souvenirs on the way home, too.

169
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,600
And we've got the Chief's brandy, too.

170
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:55,820
This is going to be a lavish party.

171
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:57,840
We didn't come here to throw a party,

172
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:59,760
we came to watch sumo.

173
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:03,220
What a fine pair of binoculars.

174
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,740
They're a must-have for watching the match.

175
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:07,100
The Chief is smart.

176
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:09,100
Let me see, let me see,
just let me see for a sec.

177
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:10,560
Wait, wait, I'm first!

178
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:14,280
Who do you think got us such great seats?

179
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:16,300
Here we go again.

180
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:18,580
Fine, fine, I'll let you look.

181
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,480
Thanks, thanks.

182
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:25,700
Figures, the people in the upper
seats haven't eaten anything decent.

183
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:29,280
That's the cute blonde girl from earlier.

184
00:10:29,820 --> 00:10:32,500
If you're not going to watch the sumo,
give them back.

185
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:34,420
Sure, why not?
It's not like it's a big deal.

186
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:36,020
That's not the point.

187
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:39,380
Now, now, let's just make a toast first.

188
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:43,560
There we go.

189
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:50,800
Aren't we forgetting something? Like a toast of thanks to Ryotsu-sensei,
or something.

190
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:56,840
Isn't that what you'd normally do?
Something good like that, right?

191
00:10:57,400 --> 00:11:04,440
Wait, wait. This person says she isn't feeling well and is heading home early, so the souvenirs are settled.
We've got plenty of room, I'm telling you.

192
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:09,060
To Ryotsu-sensei,
with heartfelt thanks, cheers!

193
00:11:14,780 --> 00:11:17,231
And now, Yokozuna Ishikata,

194
00:11:17,281 --> 00:11:20,200
Takanoyama,
making his ring-entering ceremony.

195
00:11:20,460 --> 00:11:23,360
Look, look! It's Takanoyama! Takanoyama!

196
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,780
Yeah, seeing him live,
you can really tell how taut his body is.

197
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:30,360
I'm looking forward to the final bout.

198
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:31,160
Yes, indeed.

199
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:32,956
Two yokozuna in their prime,

200
00:11:33,006 --> 00:11:35,900
what kind of great
technique will they show us?

201
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:37,040
I can't wait!

202
00:11:37,820 --> 00:11:40,400
I see, so this is the makunouchi bento

203
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:43,740
Why don't you calm down
and watch the sumo properly?

204
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:45,440
I skipped lunch.

205
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:49,200
Mind if I eat Reiko's share of the sushi?

206
00:11:50,340 --> 00:11:51,060
Sure.

207
00:11:51,420 --> 00:11:51,920
Thanks.

208
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:55,220
Senpai, he's eating in silence.

209
00:11:55,740 --> 00:11:59,380
It's fine, it's fine. It's better
to keep him quiet by feeding him.

210
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:05,060
Mayunoumi

211
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:09,260
Mayunoumi

212
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:13,460
Mayunoumi's got double
digits riding on this,

213
00:12:13,460 --> 00:12:14,980
he's really fired up, isn't he.

214
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:18,360
Unlike on TV, you can really feel
his fighting spirit, can't you?

215
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:20,880
Yoi, got it, got it.

216
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:22,480
Yes, there, there!

217
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:23,340
Go for it, go for it!

218
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:24,480
Hey, that's outrageous.

219
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:25,220
Go for it, go for it!

220
00:12:25,220 --> 00:12:26,620
I said it's outrageous, you know.

221
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,180
What? Be quiet.

222
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:30,280
This yakitori is for the outrageous part,
you know.

223
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:34,120
Don't go calling the priest
over every little thing.

224
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:36,040
Damn it!

225
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:38,540
It's already over.

226
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:40,840
Mayunoumi!

227
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:43,600
What an amazing move!

228
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:44,620
Well done!

229
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:46,740
I've never seen that before!

230
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:50,340
You idiot, we didn't get to see the match!

231
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:53,000
But you'd get mad if we ate without saying anything,
wouldn't you?

232
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,820
You'd get angry over something like that?

233
00:12:54,820 --> 00:12:56,720
Honestly, you really are something.

234
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:58,220
You're so fussy about the bill, though!

235
00:12:58,640 --> 00:12:59,460
What did you say?!

236
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:09,380
Tch, forget it. I'm going to the toilet.
Honestly, what a guy.

237
00:13:09,380 --> 00:13:19,760
Well, of course you're making a fuss over missing the first bout.
Chief, we were looking forward to Mayunoumi's match.
You can just watch that on TV when you get home.

238
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:23,160
What's the big deal?
Then what did we even come here for?

239
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:29,900
Hey, who do you think you're getting this from? You're bringing that up again.
The lottery consolation prize was kimchi, right?

240
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:41,140
In the end, I'm the one who has
to look after everything, aren't I?

241
00:13:48,220 --> 00:13:49,320
Who are you?

242
00:13:49,980 --> 00:13:52,080
Sorry. Are you all right?

243
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:57,060
Pickpocketing has been on the rise lately,
so be careful.

244
00:13:57,280 --> 00:13:57,640
Yes.

245
00:13:58,220 --> 00:14:01,380
I'm sorry. Are you hurt?

246
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:02,840
Wh-wh-wh-what?

247
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:06,040
I'm fine. Nothing, nothing.

248
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:09,240
I see. I'm really sorry.

249
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:39,200
That's strange.

250
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:43,880
I was sure we came out
somewhere around here.

251
00:14:49,580 --> 00:14:50,720
This is a problem.

252
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:54,620
Every entrance looks exactly the same.

253
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:55,900
Is something wrong?

254
00:14:57,340 --> 00:15:01,220
Well, I've lost track of my seat.

255
00:15:01,220 --> 00:15:02,120
Chief.

256
00:15:02,780 --> 00:15:04,160
This way, this way.

257
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:08,640
My companions are -

258
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:09,460
I see.

259
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:13,020
There have been a lot of pickpocketing
incidents inside the hall today,

260
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:13,840
so please be careful.

261
00:15:15,060 --> 00:15:17,620
Thank you for your hard work.

262
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:23,380
Phew, I nearly got lost.

263
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:24,680
Come on, let's head back.

264
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:25,940
Hey, Ryotsu.

265
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:28,220
We're right in front
of the concession stand.

266
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:30,700
Let's pick up some souvenirs for the others.

267
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:32,980
Hurry up, will you?

268
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:35,460
The makuuchi bouts are already in the second half,
you know.

269
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:42,200
Maybe I'll go with the Dan one.

270
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:45,440
My hand hit it.

271
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:48,320
Takamiyama's are big, as expected.

272
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:51,260
Yes, this one's not bad at all.

273
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:55,180
If it's Wakataka merchandise, it'll
sell for a good price to the women too.

274
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:58,500
This gunbai is really well made.

275
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:01,040
I'll buy one as a souvenir to take home too.

276
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:03,560
Excuse me, how much is this?

277
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:07,460
Chief, is something wrong?

278
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:09,420
My wallet's gone.

279
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:10,780
That's strange.

280
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:11,780
I'm sure I had it.

281
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:14,080
Ugh, this is just like me.

282
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:16,920
Didn't you leave it at home
and come out without it?

283
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:18,440
No way.

284
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:21,300
I bought a ticket and rode the train,
so I must have had it.

285
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:22,460
Well, there's nothing to be done.

286
00:16:22,460 --> 00:16:24,380
I'll lend you some.

287
00:16:24,380 --> 00:16:26,340
But I'm charging interest.

288
00:16:26,340 --> 00:16:27,900
What's this?

289
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:30,460
This isn't my wallet!

290
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:33,660
That's mine...

291
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:35,360
Isn't it my wallet?

292
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:37,500
W-wait a minute.

293
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:39,920
A woman's wallet?

294
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:42,460
Pickpocket! Pickpocket!
Somebody, come quick!

295
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:44,840
I-idiot! No! It's not like that!

296
00:16:45,260 --> 00:16:46,140
Where's the pickpocket?!

297
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:48,920
This is the one! He's the pickpocket!

298
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,080
I keep telling you it's not me!

299
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:51,340
Come on!

300
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:53,880
Chief, let's run!

301
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:54,060
Whoa, whoa!

302
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:56,300
Stop!

303
00:16:57,060 --> 00:16:58,880
You two over there, stop!

304
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:00,420
Stop right there!

305
00:17:00,460 --> 00:17:03,260
But why do I have to run too?

306
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,580
Ryotsu, what's going on?

307
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:06,600
What on earth is this?

308
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:09,160
Don't ask me, I have no idea either.

309
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:15,360
That's right, it was then!

310
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:18,540
You pinned that cedar-pollen crap on me,
you bastard!

311
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:20,220
Damn it!

312
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:22,240
Where the hell are you?

313
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:26,200
Ryotsu, explain yourself, Ryotsu.

314
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:26,880
Get back here!

315
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:31,320
This is bad.
At this rate, we'll both get caught.

316
00:17:32,180 --> 00:17:35,580
Chief, for the sake of justice,
please sacrifice yourself a little.

317
00:17:35,860 --> 00:17:37,100
W-what did you say?

318
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:39,500
It's a flying saucer.

319
00:17:39,620 --> 00:17:40,600
There, there.

320
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:41,480
Where, where, where?

321
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,040
Sorry, excuse me.

322
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:45,620
Whoa, hey, get back here!

323
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:52,080
They're both taking so long, aren't they?

324
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:53,700
I wonder what they're doing.

325
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:56,900
They're not lost together, are they?

326
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:59,840
With those two, it's entirely possible.
That's scary.

327
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:02,580
Should I go look for them?

328
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:05,160
Never mind, they'll be back eventually.

329
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:08,960
Besides, this is our only
chance to eat our bento in peace.

330
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:09,640
Yes, you're right.

331
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:12,880
Hey, you!

332
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,300
Ryo-chan!

333
00:18:15,660 --> 00:18:16,580
What are they doing?

334
00:18:16,620 --> 00:18:18,040
Move! Move! Move! Move!

335
00:18:20,860 --> 00:18:21,540
This is bad!

336
00:18:21,780 --> 00:18:22,900
Excuse me!

337
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:27,000
Let's go!

338
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:31,160
This is the pickpocket!

339
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:32,980
No! That's not it!

340
00:18:33,200 --> 00:18:34,880
But he's definitely one of them, isn't he!

341
00:18:35,020 --> 00:18:36,000
I keep telling you, I'm not!

342
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:39,140
Ugh! Seriously! You're so dense!

343
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:41,660
Where is he? Where is he? That blond guy!

344
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:47,720
He sacrificed the Chief.

345
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:51,200
Wherever he runs, we'll catch him!

346
00:18:52,120 --> 00:18:53,540
Whoa! There he is!

347
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:57,460
Sir, are you all right?

348
00:18:57,880 --> 00:18:59,140
Oh, y-yes.

349
00:19:00,780 --> 00:19:03,220
A pickpocket! That guy's a pickpocket!

350
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:04,620
Oh my gosh!

351
00:19:05,180 --> 00:19:06,360
Arrest him! Arrest him!

352
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:08,560
Stop!

353
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:10,340
Senpai!

354
00:19:11,060 --> 00:19:12,080
Help, help!

355
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:13,080
Stop right there!

356
00:19:13,460 --> 00:19:15,020
Easy, easy! What's going on?

357
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:22,220
Got you, you pickpocket!

358
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:24,700
Over here! We're not letting him get away!

359
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:25,900
Hey!

360
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:29,500
This guy!

361
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:31,520
Oriaa!

362
00:19:33,700 --> 00:19:35,460
Get your dirty hands off me!

363
00:19:35,780 --> 00:19:39,120
Shut up! You've been caught red-handed picking pockets,
and I'm arresting you!

364
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:40,480
Come quietly!

365
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:43,773
What are you talking about?
You're the pickpocket here, you know,

366
00:19:43,823 --> 00:19:46,280
Let go of that young lady right now!

367
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:50,000
Hey, let go!
The pickpocket is this blonde woman!

368
00:19:50,740 --> 00:19:52,940
A beauty like this couldn't possibly be a pickpocket,
you idiot!

369
00:19:52,940 --> 00:19:55,500
You're the one with the crook's face!

370
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:56,760
Don't judge people by their faces!

371
00:19:56,760 --> 00:19:58,940
This gentleman isn't a pickpocket.

372
00:19:58,940 --> 00:20:00,920
He was trying to help me.

373
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:03,640
The pickpocket is that woman over there!

374
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:04,360
That's right, that's right!

375
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:05,680
But...

376
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:08,600
What are you talking about?
Where's the proof?

377
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:12,000
Hold on a second.

378
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,380
What are you doing?

379
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:18,560
Look, that's my coin purse!

380
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:23,740
Ryotsu!

381
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:25,920
You... you...

382
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:27,240
You abandoned me!

383
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:30,180
Now, now, now. To catch the culprit,

384
00:20:30,180 --> 00:20:32,560
a little sacrifice is unavoidable, isn't it?

385
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:34,120
Besides, look how much you ran!

386
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:36,360
That must have fixed your
lack of exercise, right?

387
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:40,480
No way.

388
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:45,260
What? So many of them?

389
00:20:45,260 --> 00:20:47,420
Did you charge it all to my tab?

390
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,200
With a face that cute,
she sure knows how to pull this off.

391
00:20:53,140 --> 00:20:55,060
That's... that's my wallet!

392
00:20:55,060 --> 00:20:57,820
Honestly,
you can't let your guard down for a second.

393
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:59,800
Don't ask me.

394
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:16,760
Good grief, you're always causing
nothing but trouble, aren't you?

395
00:21:18,560 --> 00:21:19,900
Is that really fair, Chief?

396
00:21:20,540 --> 00:21:22,280
Well, I'm certainly

397
00:21:22,280 --> 00:21:24,420
a man who causes trouble all the time,

398
00:21:24,420 --> 00:21:26,700
but at least I'm not the kind of man

399
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:27,460
who's such a klutz that
his wallet gets picked.

400
00:21:27,460 --> 00:21:29,640
Can you really say that?

401
00:21:30,020 --> 00:21:32,060
With a pile of wallets
stuffed into your pocket

402
00:21:32,060 --> 00:21:33,340
and you didn't even notice?

403
00:21:33,340 --> 00:21:34,460
What did you say?

404
00:21:35,320 --> 00:21:35,640
Grr.

405
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:38,720
Ow

406
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:40,540
The sumo will be over.

407
00:21:40,860 --> 00:21:42,120
Chief, hurry!

408
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:45,020
All that's left is the
final bout of the day.

409
00:21:45,500 --> 00:21:47,240
It's the championship
playoff between two yokozuna.

410
00:21:48,620 --> 00:21:50,420
We have to at least see that much.

411
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:52,340
Ryotsu, we'll talk later!

412
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:55,680
Hurry up!
It's the best match of the tournament!

413
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:57,160
We're going to see it no matter what!

414
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:00,580
You came here on my ticket, remember?

415
00:22:01,020 --> 00:22:03,040
He's completely forgotten!

416
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:13,500
Phew, we made it in time after all.

417
00:22:14,680 --> 00:22:16,080
If we can at least watch this bout,

418
00:22:16,080 --> 00:22:18,480
then it was worth coming
all the way to the Kokugikan.

419
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:20,220
Go, go!

420
00:22:20,220 --> 00:22:21,240
There, there!

421
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:24,260
What? I can't see anything!

422
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:26,000
Senpai.

423
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:27,000
Over here.

424
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:28,400
We can't see a thing, can we?

425
00:22:29,620 --> 00:22:31,840
The big match we've been waiting for

426
00:22:36,240 --> 00:22:37,220
What happened?

427
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:39,140
It's over.

428
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:42,080
We'll never get to see this
with our own eyes again.

429
00:22:42,080 --> 00:22:43,400
It was a real showdown.

430
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:08,660
There are plenty of people around,
but you keep nitpicking every little thing.

431
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:11,100
What did you say?

432
00:23:11,100 --> 00:23:15,060
How dare you!

433
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:16,160
What do you mean?

434
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:18,660
You're fired, you bastard.

435
00:23:18,660 --> 00:23:19,880
I'll have you fired.

436
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:22,220
Isn't that going a bit too far, Chief?

437
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:23,140
Shut up.

438
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:25,200
Getting fired is only what you deserve,
isn't it?

439
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:26,100
What did you just say?

440
00:23:27,020 --> 00:23:28,120
What the hell is this -

441
00:23:28,120 --> 00:23:29,260
What?

442
00:23:29,260 --> 00:23:31,440
The climax is starting over here too!

443
00:23:31,440 --> 00:23:32,540
For crying out loud.

444
00:23:32,540 --> 00:23:33,640
Don't lose over here either!

445
00:23:35,960 --> 00:24:01,860


446
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:06,439
Red means stop, blue means go,

447
00:24:06,489 --> 00:24:09,000
let's raise our hands when
crossing the crosswalk.

448
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:11,200
What? You're saying that's common sense?

449
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:13,860
Are you all actually
following that common sense?

450
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:17,200
Alright,
I'll teach you all about traffic safety.

451
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:20,180
Next time: derailment,
runaway, full-on rampage!

452
00:24:20,580 --> 00:24:21,300
See you next time, okay?

453
00:24:32,300 --> 00:24:40,960
Let's always keep smiling,
even when something outrageous happens.

454
00:24:40,960 --> 00:24:50,700
Keep smiling cutely,
and just head out with a casual face.

455
00:24:50,700 --> 00:24:57,560
Hey, smile for me. It's not your fault.

456
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:05,840
Hey, smile for me,
like you were a moment ago.

457
00:25:05,840 --> 00:25:16,680
Keep smiling all the time, because a
woman with a serious face isn't beautiful.

458
00:25:16,680 --> 00:25:21,420
You should smile right away.

459
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:25,900
Unless you're a child, that is.

